Komika Hand (KomikaHand-Regular / -Italic / -Bold / -BoldItalic)

Copyright (c) 1999-2001 WolfBainX & Apostrophic Labs. All rights reserved.
(from the fonts' own name tables)

The Komika family was published by Apostrophic Laboratories as freeware:
the foundry released all of its fonts free of charge for personal and
commercial use and permitted their free redistribution. The foundry has
since dissolved; the fonts remain distributed as freeware by the usual
archives (Font Squirrel, DaFont) under that grant. The files here are
unmodified originals, renamed only (komika.hand.ttf -> KomikaHand-Regular.ttf
and so on) so the four styles sort as one family beside the other shipped
faces.

Shipped for the Comics app's lettering. The family covers Western-European
Latin only; text in other scripts falls back per character to the other
shipped faces (see de/comics.py).
